      "transcript": "Youshow me what you can doNoxI will build a spring experiment, measure its motion, double the mass, and compare. This is my built-in demonstration, using the real physics solver without an AI call.NoxThe mass is attached to a spring and starts one meter from equilibrium. I am measuring the original oscillation.NoxI measured an original period of 1.57 seconds. I will return to the same starting position and double the mass for the comparison.NoxThe heavier mass takes 2.22 seconds per oscillation, compared with 1.57 seconds before. Those numbers come from the actual simulation samples. The solid line is the edited run; the dashed line is the original baseline.NoxI saved the experiment, both measured runs and the baseline in this browser. You can ask me to create a pendulum, run it, select a part, change its mass, compare, or save. For a custom system, tell me what you want to build.",
